<title>USA: Alfacell president resigns.</title>
<headline>Alfacell president resigns.</headline>
<dateline>BLOOMFIELD, N.J. 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alfacell Corp said on Monday its president, Michael Lowe, resigned.</p>
<p>Strategic and daily business operations would remain the responsibility of the company chief executive, Kuslima Shogen and chief financial officer Gail Fraser, Alfacell said.</p>
<p>The resignation was mutually agreed upon by Lowe and the company, Alfacell said.</p>
<p>Alfacell develops ribonucleases for therapeutic applications and is testing an investigational antitumor agent against solid tumors in various clinical trials.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
